    <noscript><section class="no-script"><h2>Research observations</h2><p>Human Simulacra found that self-reported personality and observed behavior can move in opposite directions. Notes2Skills showed that reliable compilation can preserve incorrect model extraction. MemPot reported strong aggregate detection alongside missed and delayed detections.</p><p><a href="https://proceedings.iclr.cc/paper_files/paper/2025/file/1de176cfe0d9a288bc97faa574d7197c-Paper-Conference.pdf" rel="noreferrer noopener">Human Simulacra</a> · <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.11897v2" rel="noreferrer noopener">Notes2Skills</a> · <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.07517v1" rel="noreferrer noopener">MemPot</a></p><p>Enable JavaScript for local search and interactive graphs. No account required. Search runs in your browser.</p></section></noscript>
